{"id":"word:hebrew:H3972","type":"word","title":"מְאוּמָה","subtitle":"H3972 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, a speck or point , i.e. (by implication) something; with negative, nothing","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מְאוּמָה (H3972) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: x.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 32 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מְאוּמָה (mᵉʼûwmâh) means properly, a speck or point , i.e. (by implication) something; with negative, nothing First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 10 21."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מְאוּמָה","transliteration":"mᵉʼûwmâh","pronunciation":"meh-oo'-maw","strong":"H3972","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3972","partOfSpeech":"x","forms":["מְא֔וּמָה","מְא֑וּמָה","מְאֽוּמָה","לִ/מְאֽוּמָה","מְא֖וּמָה"],"morphs":[["HNcfsa",28],["HR/Ncfsa",2],["HC/Ncfsa",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, a speck or point , i.e. (by implication) something; with negative, nothing","usage":"fault, no(-ught), ought, somewhat, any (no-)thing.","full":"H3972. meumah מְא֫וּמָה 32 pronoun indefinite anything (according to Thes from וּמָה מָה , like quidquid , against which is the Mil`el tone; according to Ol 254, 255, 386 Kö ii. 146 an old accusative from מאוּם in sense of speck, particle , compare French point: in Assyrian manman (properly who ? who ? ), assimilated mamman , or manma ( man, who ? + Generalizing ma ), mamma , is any one, minma ( min, what ? + ma ), mimma , is anything , Dl § 60, HWB 418 f ; W SG 125 f. ); — anything , usually in negative sentences, as Gen 22:12 מאומה לו ואלתֿעשׂ (euphem. for something bad ), 30:31 לֹאתִֿתֶּןלִֿי מאומה , 39:6 , 9 ; 40:15 (euphemism), 1Sam 12:4-5 , 20:26 , 39 ; 25:7 , 15 , 21 ; 29:3 etc., Judg 14:6 בידו אין ומאומה , Eccl 5:14 ׳ומ בעמלו ישׂא לא 1Kin 18:43 מ ׳אין literally nought of anything ! Jer 39:12 רָּע מאומה לו תעשׂ ואל ; strengthened by כֹּל Gen 39:23 ; 2Sam 3:35 ; after אִם = surely not , 3:35 ; in interrogative sentence Num 22:38 ; in affirm. sentence Deut 24:10 מ מַשֵּׁאת ׳בְרֵעֲךָ כִּיתַֿשֶּׁה a pledge of (= consisting in) anything , 2Sam 13:2 (euphemism), 2Kin 5:20 . Used adverbially, 1Sam 21:3 מ ידע אל ׳אישׁ הדבר את let no one know of the matter in anything at all . מָאוֺר , [ מְאוּרָה ] see אור . [ מאזן ], מאֹזְנַיִם see II. אזן .","rootNote":"apparently a form of 3971 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 10 21","keyReferences":["1Kgs 10 21","1Kgs 18 43","1Sam 12 4","1Sam 12 5","1Sam 20 26","1Sam 20 39","1Sam 21 3","1Sam 25 7"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":32,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 10 21","book":"1Kgs","chapter":10,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לִ/מְאֽוּמָה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncfsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 18 43","book":"1Kgs","chapter":18,"verse":43,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מְא֑וּמָה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 12 4","book":"1Sam","chapter":12,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מְאֽוּמָה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 12 5","book":"1Sam","chapter":12,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מְא֑וּמָה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 20 26","book":"1Sam","chapter":20,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מְא֖וּמָה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 20 39","book":"1Sam","chapter":20,"verse":39,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מְא֑וּמָה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 21 3","book":"1Sam","chapter":21,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מְא֛וּמָה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 25 7","book":"1Sam","chapter":25,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מְא֔וּמָה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 25 15","book":"1Sam","chapter":25,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מְא֔וּמָה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"